# kk-collect — standalone 6-hourly collection (04:00/10:00/16:00/22:00 local) into the kk store.
#
# Rendered by `kk schedule render kk-collect --platform cron --repo <checkout>`; kk never edits
# the operator's crontab. Operator action (plugins/kk/README.md §Schedule) — MERGE, never replace:
#
#     crontab -l > /tmp/kk-collect.cron 2>/dev/null || :
#     kk schedule render kk-collect --platform cron --repo "$PWD" >> /tmp/kk-collect.cron
#     crontab /tmp/kk-collect.cron
#
# `kk store lock` is the single-flight guard, so an overlapping tick exits 0 without collecting.
#
# `mkdir -p` + an explicit PATH are load-bearing, not decoration: cron runs with a minimal PATH (no
# `spur`/`kk`/`jq`/`bun`) and its `>>` redirect fails on a missing directory BEFORE the command runs,
# so a bare line would produce no log and no tick. The README install steps mirror this.
#
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY is bound by `kk schedule render` from the environment it runs in, for the same
# reason PATH is: `kk store label` consults the `typesafe` decision maker, spur keeps that credential
# env-only, and cron inherits nothing from the operator's shell — without it every typesafe label
# degrades to its fail-closed default and the daily pool comes back empty (2026-10-12).
#
# shortcut: the value is single-quoted verbatim, so it must not contain a literal `'` — true of the
# apikey_<hex>_<hex> form; escape it here (or move to a wrapper script) if a credential ever can.
0 4,10,16,22 * * * cd {{repo}} && mkdir -p .works/kk-collect && PATH="{{home}}/.bun/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin" TYPESAFE_API_KEY='{{typesafe_api_key}}' spur workflow run plugins/kk/workflows/kk-collect.yaml >> {{repo}}/.works/kk-collect/launchd.log 2>&1
